Start a web search operation.

This command resolves convenience flags and --input into one request body,
creates a private action record before live submission, and sends exactly one
idempotency key for the logical action. Use --dry-run for a local preview; to
request a server dry run, include "dry_run": true in the JSON body when the
operation supports it.

Paid live submissions require confirmation through --yes or an interactive
prompt. JSON output is one stable object with action, remote operation and
recovery fields. Use --plain to print the accepted operation id or action id.
In --no-prompt or non-interactive mode, use --yes to acknowledge paid live
work. When the operation schema supports dry_run, an input body with
"dry_run": true performs authenticated server validation without creating a
local action record or sending an idempotency key. Pass --idempotency-key to
supply a caller-owned replay key for live work.

Related commands:
  chab operations schema search.web
  chab operations resume

Usage:
  chab search web [flags]

Examples:
  chab search web --query 'best coffee grinder' --engine google --location '{"country":"US"}' --language en --yes
  chab search web --input @request.json --yes --json

Flags:
      --device string            device type
      --dry-run                  preview the resolved request without resolving credentials or contacting the API
      --engine string            search engine
  -h, --help                     help for web
      --idempotency-key string   explicit idempotency key; generated when omitted
      --input string             JSON request body, @path, or @- for stdin
      --language string          language code
      --limit int                result limit
      --location string          location object as JSON
      --max-credits int          set max_credit_budget for supported operations
      --query string             search query
      --safe-search string       safe search setting
      --set stringArray          top-level request field as name=json (repeatable)
      --wait                     wait for an accepted operation to reach a terminal state

Global Flags:
      --api-base-url string   API base URL (Chab default uses www.chab.ai/v1; custom base URLs use <base-url>/v1)
      --auth-file string      path to the CLI auth file
      --base-url string       product web base URL
      --config string         path to the CLI config file
      --debug                 write redacted request details to stderr
      --include-meta          include safe response metadata in machine output where supported
      --jq string             filter supported JSON output with a jq expression
      --json                  print stable JSON output where supported
      --locale string         response language sent as Accept-Language (en or de)
      --no-ansi               disable ANSI terminal controls and paging where supported
      --no-color              disable color in human output where supported
      --no-pager              disable pager use for long human output where supported
      --no-prompt             fail instead of prompting for interactive input
      --plain                 print copy-safe plain output where supported
      --profile string        profile to use for this invocation
      --template string       render supported JSON output with a Go text/template
      --yes                   accept supported confirmations for risky or destructive operations; does not supply missing input
